direction: right
title: Spark Data Abstractions Evolution

RDD: RDD (Low-Level JVM Objects) {
  style.stroke: "#64748B"
  R_type: Opaque JVM objects (RDD[T])
  R_opt: No Catalyst optimization
  R_gc: High GC overhead & memory churn
  R_py: Very slow in PySpark (Pickle serialization)
}

DataFrame: DataFrame (Relational Table Schema) {
  style.stroke: "#34D399"
  D_type: Untyped Relational Rows (Dataset[Row])
  D_opt: Full Catalyst Optimizer & CBO
  D_gc: Tungsten off-heap memory (Zero GC overhead)
  D_py: Native speed in PySpark (Identical to Scala)
}

Dataset: Dataset (Strongly Typed JVM Objects) {
  style.stroke: "#C084FC"
  S_type: Strongly typed JVM case classes (Dataset[T])
  S_opt: Catalyst optimization + compile-time type safety
  S_gc: Efficient Encoders to Tungsten format
  S_py: Scala / Java only (Not in Python)
}

RDD -> DataFrame: Schema Enforced & Tungsten Memory { style.stroke: "#34D399" }
DataFrame -> Dataset: Compile-Time Type Safety (Scala) { style.stroke: "#C084FC" }
